lines=['# Content-quality audit: candidate verification and finding disposition','','**Assessment kind:** owner-selected documentation content quality, using Document Analysis.','**Assessor:** Codex worker /root, also author of the repairs; this is a disclosed worker content assessment, not independent Project Audit.','**Authority:** D-000012; requirements fixed in S-000002/E-000008 before edits/checks.','**Baseline:** [R-000007 content report](../R-000007/content-audit.md); exact before and after under C-000004.','**Candidate:** all 71 maintained files in C-000004 after snapshot; 64 public Markdown documents, 500 declared current headings/preambles/whole-file units. Changed-paths.json identifies 27 edited documents. Unit-count reduction reflects rewritten outlines and fence-aware parsing; no maintained file was removed.','','## Scope, reading and provenance','','Manual review read the primary entry documents and the complete method/architecture/records/role guides, original context, full relevant concepts, changed documents and their diff against the frozen baseline. All remaining public Markdown openings/headings and routing were inspected; specialised unchanged procedures were consulted for the process promises below. This is an orientation/coherence audit, not a sentence-by-sentence legal, scientific or code-correctness audit of every unchanged document. Mechanical inventories supplement the declared semantic reading, never expand it. Exact quoted candidate text below is extracted from the retained after source.','','## Requirement-to-current-text assessment','']
